      "usedFor": "Literature review defining Cypriotism (Mavratsas, Peristianis, Panayiotou, Attalides, Kizilyurek): independence from both motherlands, a de-ethnicised Cypriot identity, opposition to Greek and Turkish Cypriot nationalism and to partition, support for federal reunification on both sides."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "kind": "scholarly",
      "title": "Cypriotism as nationalism: a study of Cypriotist discourse (PhD thesis, University of Warwick)",
      "author": "Antonis Pastellopoulos",
      "url": "https://wrap.warwick.ac.uk/id/eprint/182675/7/WRAP_Theses_Pastellopoulos_2023.pdf",
      "usedFor": "Chapters 2, 4, 5 and 8, read in full text: the definition of Cypriotism, its treatment of Turkish Cypriots as a political community of equal stature, and its case for bi-communal federation with entrenched communal autonomy and rejection of majoritarianism, from Cypriotist magazines and a blog 1999-2020 (Greek Cypriot left and anti-authoritarian circles)."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
