    {
      "text": "The two main communities of a divided country should be recognised as political communities of equal standing, not as a majority and a minority.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Cypriotist discourse represents Turkish Cypriots as a political community of equal stature to Greek Cypriots and rejects their treatment as a minority.",
      "sources": [
